WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.403
-Our first guests tonight
are very funny comedians

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.238
and "New York Times"
best-selling writers.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.573
The third season of their
fantastic show, "Desus &amp; Mero,"

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:10.309
premieres January 31st
on Showtime.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:13.846
Please welcome back to the show
Desus Nice and The Kid Mero!

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.715
How are you, gentlemen?
-Hey.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.516
-Hey, Seth!
-Hey, Seth! Ha!

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:19.819
Good to be here.
-Thanks for having us back!

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.988
-Guys, it is --
it is so good to see you.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.823
And I'm gonna ask you
the question

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.392
every talk-show host has asked.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.727
How do you think
comedy will be affected

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.228
by the Biden administration?

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.631
And how have you felt
about the first week?

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.733
-Oh, I thought we were here

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.370
to do the new --
the new Chinese swab.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.606
-You guys were
gonna do the swab?

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.509
-I thought that's --
That's what they told us

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.943
in the -- in the pre thing.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.846
-We're not doing
the new Chinese swab!

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.415
-You're not gonna --
We're not doing that?

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.782
I was kind of
looking forward to it.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.851
-We were --
If you were here in person.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.520
But being remote, it would
have to be such a long swab.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.291
-Yeah. An extendo.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:03.195
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.264
But so far --
I mean, so far, Biden --

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.834
You know, Biden's doing well.
It's like -- It's --

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.101
He's the new guy on the job.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.703
He had to get
the WiFi passwords.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.474
You know, he's still probably
fumigating the Oval Office.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.142
People forget that when Trump
left, they stole a lot of stuff.

00:01:17.142 --> 00:01:19.178
They might have stole
all the ethernet cable.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.946
They might have took
all the silverware.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.115
There's probably, like, keys
missing on the MacBook.

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:24.751
They're starting from scratch,
so, you know, give him

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.586
a little slack.
Give him a month at least.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.920
-Yeah.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.922
-And, Biden, he's got
a lot to do, like you said.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.958
He's signing executive orders
at a breakneck pace.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:35.261
You know what I mean? He's --
He's still Febrezing stuff.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.330
You know what I mean?
Give him a little while

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.899
to, you know, mess up,
and then we'll --

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.867
"Yah!" Get him.
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.137
-I wanted to ask you guys
if you enjoyed watching

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.573
the inauguration,
especially because the Bronx

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.775
represented itself so well.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:52.478
Not just with Sonia Sotomayor,
but with -- with Jennifer Lopez.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:53.780
-Yes.
-With Queen J.Lo.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.715
That's right.
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.183
Shout-out to Biden doing
inauguration the right way,

00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:00.753
having actual guests,
having actual musicians

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.423
people wanted to see.
-Yes, absolutely!

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:06.625
-As a Bronx resident,
I got nervous 'cause I saw

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.027
the look in J.Lo's eyes.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.896
She thought
she was back in Vegas.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.864
She was about to go
into a rendition

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.232
of "Waiting For Tonight" or --

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.234
I don't know --
"I'm just Jenny from the block."

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.736
I know Secret Service was like,
"Enough. Enough. Turn it off."

00:02:17.736 --> 00:02:20.539
-You know -- But, yeah, no.
Shout-out to J.Lo.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:23.576
Her -- Her valiant attempt
to sing

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.778
was well-recognized.
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.981
The only thing missing
was that Versace dress.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.150
-And shout-out to her sneaking
in that "Let's get loud."

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.452
That's what the nation needs.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.953
We're gonna start putting that
on our currency.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.889
"Let's get loud."
-♪ Let's get loud ♪

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.925
-How do you feel --
Are you optimistic

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.927
about the working relationship
between Vice President Harris

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.395
and President Biden?

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:46.432
-Mm-hmm. That should be
an easy -- That's a lay-up.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:51.137
Especially because right now the
barometer -- the bar is so low.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.172
It's like --
how bad can a presidential

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.940
and vice-president
relationship be?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.477
The last president tried to have
the vice president murdered.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.746
So as long as Joe Biden
doesn't do that,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.215
I think everything
will be hunky-dory over there.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.484
-They could slap-box
on Instagram Live,

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.352
and it would
still not be as bad.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.588
-Well, so, you mentioned
both social media

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.590
and the insurrection
at the Capitol.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.626
Are you surprised how easy
it's been for the FBI

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.796
to sort of find and apprehend
so many of these people,

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.465
who basically posted their --
their crime on --

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.467
on social media
as they were doing it?

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.869
-You know what?
They're saying that these people

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.805
don't believe
that blue lives matter.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.441
Clearly they do because
they went out there to make it

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.510
as easy as possible
for blue lives to find them.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.912
They tagged their posts.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.247
They put on the GPS
on the videos.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:37.550
They're doing -- They're
doing Braille translations

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.819
of some of their photos
just to make sure everyone

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.221
can see what they're doing.
It's -- It's mind-blowing.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.558
-Bro, they were taking selfies
with the cops.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.159
Like, "Hey, this is gonna --

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.694
Just so you remember,
this is me.

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:51.664
This is my face. My name
is Edward. Nice to meet you.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.733
I'm gonna steal some stuff
from Pelosi's office."

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.068
-Yeah, it seemed like a lot
of those people, it was maybe

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:59.905
their first crime based on
how many mistakes they made.

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:01.874
-It was big high-school energy.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.410
The first time you shoplifted,
and you're gonna document it.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.379
"Look what I took from Sephora!

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.947
Oh, my God!
I'm out of control!"

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.316
Like, no!
"Grandma, get out the Capitol!"

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:13.619
-"I stole golf tees!
I don't even golf!"

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:16.288
-Hey, uh, speaking of golf,
how do you think life --

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:19.158
What do you think life is like
for former President Trump

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.059
right now in Mar-a-Lago?

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:23.495
-Miserable. Miserable.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:25.164
'Cause he doesn't have Twitter
anymore.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.800
That was his life.
That was his pride and joy.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.801
Not his kids.
Not any of his hotels.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.770
Twitter.
And now he has no Twitter.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.440
He has all of these people
talking about him on TV.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.476
He has no way
to get his opinion out.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.711
Now he's that guy
that you avoid at every bar.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.013
He's, like, kind of drunk
at the end of the bar,

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.282
and he has an opinion
that he's just saying out loud

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:45.852
that he wants somebody to hear,
but nobody wants to hear it.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.087
He's probably
walking around Mar-a-Lago

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.489
just writing tweets
on, like, Post-It notes

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:53.593
and sticking them on random
places, hoping people find them.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.194
-He's on the back nine right now

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.796
talking to an alligator
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:00.933
-He's like "Yo,
you see what Biden did?

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.769
He's terrible.
I was the best president ever."

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.303
-"Look at him,
look at him, look at him.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.105
Don't you agree with me,
Mr. Chompers?

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.775
Biden's an awful leader.
He's not a real leader."

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.277
-Guys, what about a question --

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.245
Another question
we've all been asked.

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:16.149
People have said Donald Trump
was good for comedy.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:19.718
Now that it's over, are you --
are you worried, or do you think

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:21.820
you're going to be just fine,
if not better?

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.122
-No, it's true.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.291
-No. Now we actually
have to do our jobs.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.860
We actually have to, like, study
and be comedians.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.064
Before, it was like a lay-up
line. You know what I mean?

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:33.232
The warm-up
before the actual game.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.401
'Cause it's such
low-hanging fruit.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:38.838
This guy did something dumb
every 48 hours.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.940
So now it's like, you know,

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.176
we have to actually,
you know, spread our wings.

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:47.713
-And that's why it's such a gift
when there's a new anal swab.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.015
-That's right.
-Yeah. Boom! There you go.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.284
-But you know what?
Honestly, the jig is up.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:56.021
Trump has exposed that
late-night comedy is a fraud.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:59.925
We meet up in the Slack with you
and Jimmy Fallon and everybody,

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.594
and we share
the same Trump jokes.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.028
Now we're done. We're done!

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.531
Trump was pumping
the late-night industry

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.733
the same way Reddit
is doing GameStop.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.535
I'm telling you!
-That's right. It's over for us.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.936
It's like
"The Wolf of Wall Street."

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.972
It's all coming crashing down!

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:15.208
-If you see me on the street,
throw some change in my hat.

